Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Edge overflow of the rolling ball fillet. Where the ball tangent to the two
faces of an edge cannot touch one of them within that face (a face narrower
than the rounding), the rounding runs onto the face beyond the narrow
face's far edge or, where the ball cannot touch that face, rolls on the far
edge (a blend on an obstacle: surface/restriction), and the narrow face
vanishes. OCCT had blends on obstacles only where a walk met an edge in the
middle of a rounding; a rounding whose contact leaves a face along the whole
edge found no start (StartsolFailure).

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSolOverflow (new, called from
  PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine when StartSol finds no start): at sections along
  the spine, the section on the faces' unbounded surfaces; where exactly one
  contact lies outside its face, the face's edge the section crosses between
  the spine and that contact and the face beyond it: a start touching that
  face (a section whose normals meet in a circle centre), else a start
  rolling on the edge, set up as StartSol sets up an obstacle met by a walk.
  Fillets only (chamfers implement no blend on an obstacle).
- PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: a blend on an obstacle that reaches the end of
  the spine, or a face at the vertex that ends it (ObstacleAtSpineEnd, new,
  with ChFi3d_ArcEndsSpine), ends the stripe there, as a blend between two
  faces does; before, the loop went on past the end.
- ChFi3d_Builder::ComputeData (edge/face): on a periodic guide a path that
  starts inside sets the period's origin where the path to the left ended,
  as the face/face ComputeData does, so that a blend rolling on a closed
  edge goes round.
- ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformSurf (both edge/face variants): a blend on an
  obstacle whose contact on its face ends on an edge of a face at the end of
  the spine is extended past it (ChFi3d_ExtendAtSpineEnds), as blends
  between two faces are, so that the face at the end cuts it.
- PerformOneCorner: the end of a blend on an obstacle lies at a vertex of
  the obstacle edge (or near it, where a section across the spine meets the
  face at the end a little before); its common point gets the edge of that
  vertex that bounds the face the blend touches and the face at the end
  (ChFi3d_ObstacleEndOnFace), so that FindFace finds the face at the end.
- ChFi3d_CutConsumedFaces (new, called after ChFi3d_FilDS): the face on the
  other side of an obstacle edge, between it and the spine, which the blend
  consumes, is dropped when it is a strip between the spine and that edge:
  its other edges at the vertices where the blend ends are cut there, so
  that nothing of it is connected to the result.
